urning `True` as soon as the loop finishes without checking the stack is empty (`((` would pass). Counting brackets instead of matching them (`([)]` has balanced counts but is invalid).\n\n**Interview follow-ups.** (1) The string also contains letters and digits; ignore them. (2) Return the minimum number of insertions to make the string valid. (3) Validate a stream too large to hold in memory: only the stack of open brackets is needed, but its depth is bounded by the nesting depth, not the input length.","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(n)"},"similar":["min-stack","generate-parentheses","longest-valid-parentheses"],"followups":["Handle other characters in the string.","Minimum insertions to make it valid."],"number":31,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def isValid(self, s: str) -> bool:\n        pass\n"}